description: Keep Cursor and AI tooling out of commit and pull request attribution
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commit and Pull Request Attribution

Never credit Cursor, or any AI tool, as an author or co-author. Commits and pull
requests belong to the person who owns the change.

## Commit messages

A commit message is a subject line plus an optional body. Nothing else.

```text
# BAD - attribution trailer
Smooth icon scaling and add native-resolution sizes

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursor@cursor.com>
```

```text
# GOOD
Smooth icon scaling and add native-resolution sizes
```

Also never add: `Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent`, `Generated with Cursor`,
`Signed-off-by: Cursor`, robot emoji footers, or notes like "AI-assisted".

`Co-authored-by` trailers naming real people are correct and must be preserved.

## Pull requests

Keep the title and body about the change: what it does, why, and how it was
verified. Do not add a line stating the PR was written by Cursor or an agent.

```text
# BAD - trailing attribution in the PR body
## Summary
Replace nearest-neighbour icon scaling with an alpha-weighted resampler.

Created by Cursor 🤖
```

Delete that last line and the body is correct. Cursor's tooling may append a run
link automatically; that is not something to add by hand.
